d get to travel  for press and be in the same room with  our co-stars and  be in the same room with you guys and  have that one-on-one experience so  perspective it's definitely made me i  think i i won't get as anxious or  nervous anymore because i miss it  it's really special to have that you  know  yeah that that's really interesting and  it's interesting too because that answer  you just gave is very genuine and real  and i think that  you also on your presence in social  media is very genuine and real  and i actually love that because you had  a tweet on january 19th that was  i def just danced around my kitchen to  one day more now  les miz is one of my fav is my favorite  play  by miles and i know you played young  cozette yeah i have to ask this question  but  if you were to play in les mis today who  would you want to play  now that you're older now that i'm older  ah man  i don't know because my voice falls  right in between eponine  and little cossette but i feel like my  soul  wants to play eponine because i just  love how  angsty her role is and how powerful her  songs are so  or maybe fontine no but epinephrine  has more songs i'm gonna go with eponine  love it  and uh that's a great pick and i think  you would totally kill it so i hope one  day it happens  um so wrapping things up going back to  the film knowing this is the final  film in this series was it really  emotional on set  is there something also that you would  take away from this experience that  you'd bring to the rest of your  career yeah man we just feel so  grateful i mean when we filmed the first  movie we we knew there were three books  but there's no guarantee that the  movie's gonna take off enough for you to  be able to do  two let alone all three movies so to  finally be here  um debuting our third movie is so  bittersweet we're so proud we can't wait  for the fans to see it  it's truly a beautiful ending to lara  jean's story  as well as a beginning to the next  chapter for life